In Python, inheritance allows one class (child / derived class) to reuse properties and methods of another class (parent / base class).
🔹 What is Inheritance?
•	One class acquires features of another class
•	Promotes code reusability
•	Supports method overriding
•	Achieves IS-A relationship
🔹 Basic Syntax
class Parent:
    def parent_method(self):
        print("This is parent class")

class Child(Parent):
    def child_method(self):
        print("This is child class")
c = Child()
c.parent_method()
c.child_method()
🔹 Example with Constructor Inheritance
class Animal:
    def __init__(self, name):
        self.name = name

    def speak(self):
        print("Animal makes sound")

class Dog(Animal):
    def __init__(self, name, breed):
        super().__init__(name)   # call parent constructor
        self.breed = breed

    def speak(self):
        print("Dog barks")
d = Dog("Tommy", "Labrador")
d.speak()
print(d.name, d.breed)
🔹 Types of Inheritance in Python
1️ Single Inheritance
class A:
    pass

class B(A):
    pass
2️ Multiple Inheritance
class A:
    def show(self):
        print("A")

class B:
    def display(self):
        print("B")

class C(A, B):
    pass
3️ Multilevel Inheritance
class A:
    pass

class B(A):
    pass

class C(B):
    pass
4 Hierarchical Inheritance
class A:
    pass

class B(A):
    pass

class C(A):
    pass
5 Hybrid Inheritance
Combination of two or more types.
🔹 super() in Inheritance
•	Calls parent class methods
•	Avoids hardcoding parent class name
class Parent:
    def show(self):
        print("Parent")

class Child(Parent):
    def show(self):
        super().show()
        print("Child")
🔹 Method Overriding
class Parent:
    def greet(self):
        print("Hello from Parent")

class Child(Parent):
    def greet(self):
        print("Hello from Child")
🔹 isinstance() & issubclass()
isinstance(obj, Class)
issubclass(Child, Parent)
🔹 Access Control in Inheritance
Modifier	Example	Access
Public	x	Everywhere
Protected	_x	Child classes
Private	__x	Same class only

🔹 Real-World Example (Employee)
class Employee:
    def __init__(self, name):
        self.name = name

    def work(self):
        print("Employee working")

class Manager(Employee):
    def manage(self):
        print("Manager managing")

